Decode a ZRLE rectangle
  Read and validate the declared compressed length against the rectangle size.
  Decode only that many compressed bytes using the connection's continuous zlib stream.
  Read up to 64 by 64 pixels per tile from left to right and top to bottom.
  Decode raw and solid pixels, packed palettes with byte-aligned rows, and plain or palette runs.
  Reject reserved tile modes, missing data, bad palette indexes, overlong runs, and surplus data.
  Copy each decoded tile into the framebuffer at the rectangle's offset.

Close the decoder
  Release the connection's inflater and its compression history.
